# Styles: which rule wins when several give the same property.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Styles · Which one wins
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		# Inside the demo only, so that the heading keeps its color.
		For style: demo
			For element: Text
				Typography:
					Color: #1F6B3A
		For style: plum
			Typography:
				Color: #6B2A5E
		For id: brick
			Typography:
				Color: #A32D2D
		For style: line
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 10 0
				Padding: 6 8
				Border: 0 0 0 3
				Border color: rule
			Typography:
				Size: 12
				Bold: true
	Section:
		Text: Styles
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Which one wins
		Paragraph: When several sources give the same property, the strongest wins: what the element declares, then its `For id` rule, its `For style` rules, its `For element` rule and finally what it inherits from its parent. Each line below adds one source of `Color` to those of the line above it.
			Style: intro
		Block:
			Style: demo
			Typography:
				Color: #8A5A00
			Text: Inherited from the Block: Color: #8A5A00
				Style: label
			Paragraph: A paragraph has no rule of its own, so it takes the color of its block.
				Style: line
			Text: For element: Text beats the inherited color
				Style: label
			Text: Green, from For element: Text
				Style: line
			Text: For style beats For element
				Style: label
			Text: Plum, from For style: plum
				Style: line plum
			Text: For id beats For style
				Style: label
			Text: Brick red, from For id: brick
				Id: brick
				Style: line plum
			Text: The element itself beats all the rules
				Style: label
			Text: Blue, declared on the Text itself
				Style: line plum
				Typography:
					Color: accent
